 "result": "I fixed it, and `test_discount_rounding` now passes, along with `test_no_discount`.\n\nThe bug was in `apply_discount` in `calc/pricing.py`. It used `int(... * 100) / 100`, which cuts off the extra digits instead of rounding. Floating-point maths makes `2.30 * 0.5 * 100` come out as 114.999\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6, so the result was cut down to 1.14 instead of 1.15.\n\nI changed the line to `return round(price * (1 - pct / 100), 2)`. The test file is unchanged.",
